**RICHLAND SCHOOL DISTRICT 88A**  
**REFERENDUM**PROPOSITION TO INCREASE THE LIMITING RATE
_Shall the limiting rate under the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law for Richland School District Number 88A, Will County, Illinois, be increased by an additional amount equal to 0.3900% above the limiting rate for levy year 2025 for school purposes, and be equal to 2.7833% of the equalized assessed value of the taxable property therein for levy year 2026?_

_(1) The approximate amount of taxes extendable at the most recently extended limiting rate is $10,891,203 and the approximate amount of taxes extendable if the proposition is approved is $12,665,978._

_(2) For the 2026 levy year the approximate amount of the additional tax extendable against property containing a single family residence and having a fair market value at the time of the referendum of $100,000 is estimated to be $130.00._

_(3) If the proposition is approved, the aggregate extension for 2026 will be determined by the limiting rate set forth in the proposition, rather than the otherwise applicable limiting rate calculated under the provisions of the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law (commonly known as the Property Tax Cap Law)._

**TROY COMMUNITY CONSOLIDATED SCHOOL DISTRICT #30-C**  
**REFERENDUM**PROPOSITION TO INCREASE THE LIMITING RATE
_Shall the limiting rate under the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law for Troy Community Consolidated School District Number 30-C, Will County, Illinois, be increased by an additional amount equal to 0.4500% above the limiting rate for levy year 2025 for the purpose of providing educational programming and instruction, operating, maintaining, constructing and improving school buildings and facilities and constructing school safety and security improvements and for other school purposes, and be equal to 3.6241 % of the equalized assessed value of the taxable property therein for levy year 2026?_

_(1) The approximate amount of taxes extendable at the most recently extended limiting rate is $57,422,051, and the approximate amount of taxes extendable if the proposition is approved is $65,562,917._

_(2) For the 2026 levy year the approximate amount of the additional tax extendable against property containing a single family residence and having a fair market value at the time of the referendum of $100,000 is estimated to be $150._

_(3) If the proposition is approved, the aggregate extension for 2026 will be determined by the limiting rate set forth in the proposition, rather than the otherwise applicable limiting rate calculated under the provisions of the Property Tax Extension Limitation Law (commonly known as the Property Tax Cap Law)._

**OSWEGO COMMUNITY UNIT SCHOOL DISTRICT  
 REFERENDUM**(Kendall, Kane, and Will Counties)  
PROPOSITION TO ISSUE $317,000,000 SCHOOL BUILDING BONDS
_Shall the Board of Education of Oswego Community Unit School District Number 308, Kendall, Kane and Will Counties, Illinois, alter, repair and equip existing school buildings and improve the sites thereof, including installation of secure entryways, access controls, intrusion detection systems, and enhanced cameras; infrastructure repairs to roofing, mechanical, plumbing, and HVAC systems; science lab improvements; expansions to shared cafeteria/gym spaces; and improvements to provide enhanced energy efficiency; and issue bonds of said School District to the amount of $317,000,000 for the purpose of paying the costs thereof?_

